BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Meet Spinnaker\, A Very Special Humpback Whale
DTSTART:20250317T000000
DTEND:20250317T020000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:3f2bedd670325fac874ee16dad564d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Spinnaker Exhibit at Center for Coastal Studies’ Hiebert Mar
 ine Laboratory in Provincetown The Center for Coastal Studies’ Hiebert M
 arine Laboratory in Provincetown is home to the Spinnaker Exhibit\, which 
 features the intact skeleton of a 34-foot humpback whale named Spinnaker. 
 Spinnaker spent much of her life in the Gulf of Maine\, and is known to ha
 ve been entangled in fishing gear at least four times during her short lif
 e. She was disentangled by the Center’s Marine Animal Entanglement Respo
 nse team three times. Despite these efforts\, the long-term effects of her
  second-known entanglement were lethal\, and she died in 2015 at the age o
 f 11. Spinnaker’s skeleton was preserved and is on permanent display at 
 the Center for Coastal Studies. She delivers a powerful message about the 
 lives of whales in the modern world. The exhibit is open Monday through Fr
 iday\, 10 am to 4 pm. Free admission\, donations welcomed. 5 Holway Avenue
 \, Provincetown.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.cap
 ecodchamber.org/event/meet-spinnaker-a-very-special-humpback-whale/38367/
LOCATION:Center for Coastal Studies\, 5 Holway Avenue\, Provincetown\, MA 
 02657\, 5 Holway Avenue\, Provincetown\, MA\, 02657
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/meet-spinnaker-a-very-special-hum
 pback-whale/38367/
END:VEVENT
