BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:AudaTours Worcester Audio Tour: Statues\, Spires & Civic Stories U
 nveiled
DTSTART:20260207T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:491991fc587a99980c8d480a4ef305@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A bronze turtle watches as legends rise and fall in Worcester
 ’s streets\, its gaze as steady as the city’s restless spirit. Behind 
 the bustle and brick lie stories lurking in plain sight-whispers of revolu
 tion\, resilience\, and reinvention. Set off on this self-guided audio tou
 r to reveal the drama etched into the DCU Center\, the strange magic cling
 ing to Burnside Fountain\, and the faded glories of Worcester Memorial Aud
 itorium. Uncover secrets in spots often hurried past and hear tales most v
 isitors never imagine. Why did a crowd once swarm these steps in desperate
  protest? What secrets echo after midnight around Turtle Boy’s pedestal?
  What scandal unraveled inside the Auditorium’s grand halls over a centu
 ry ago? Stride through echoes of parades and protests\, scandals and celeb
 rations. Every corner holds a revelation and every story lets you see Worc
 ester through new eyes. Start your journey and meet the city’s mysteries
  where they stand-turtle\, stone\, and memory intertwined.\n\nSources: Dis
 cover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.org
 /event/audatours-worcester-audio-tour%3a-statues-spires-%26-civic-stories-
 unveiled/29278/
LOCATION:St. John's Catholic Church (Worcester\, Massachusetts)\, 44 Templ
 e St\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/audatours-worcester-audio-tour
 %3a-statues-spires-%26-civic-stories-unveiled/29278/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tour The First Church of Christ\, Scientist\, Boston
DTSTART:20260208T000000
DTEND:20260208T020000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:308d8c08b7b7c0152d489fb936da15@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for free tours of the original Romanesque church (The 
 Mother Church Original\, 1894) and the Byzantine-Renaissance extension (Th
 e Mother Church Extension\, 1906)\, which houses one of the world’s larg
 est pipe organs. Tuesday: 11 a.m. Wednesday: 11 a.m.\, and 3 p.m. Thursday
 : 11 a.m.\, and 3 p.m. Friday: 11 a.m.\, 1 p.m.\, and 3 p.m. Saturday: 11 
 a.m.\, 1 p.m.\, and 3 p.m. Sunday: 1 p.m.\, and 3 p.m. Church tours begin 
 in the Welcome Hall of the How Do You See the World? experience. When you 
 arrive in the Welcome Hall\, a host can help you find the tour group meeti
 ng location. No reservations are required for church tours. When the tour 
 begins\, you will walk a short distance across the Christian Science Plaza
  to enter the church through the glass walled Portico with your tour group
 . The entire tour is wheelchair accessible. Tours may be available in lang
 uages other than English. Discounted parking is available in the Christian
  Science Plaza garage with validation. There is an accessible entrance wit
 h 24/7 elevator access to the Christian Science Plaza. Group tours For gro
 ups of 10+ people\, please fill out the request form. Questions? Contact t
 he Group Tours Coordinator at GroupVisits@christianscience.com or 617-450-
 7330. Meeting Point Address The Welcome Hall\, inside the How Do You See t
 he World? experience 210 Massachusetts Ave\, Boston\, 02115 For more infor
 mation about Church tours\, please visit christianscience.com/tours. Visit
 ors are also always welcome at Sunday services\, Sunday school\, and Wedne
 sday testimony meetings. Learn more at christianscience.com/services.\n\nS
 ources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-the
 -first-church-of-christ-scientist-boston/78407/
LOCATION:The First Church of Christ\, Scientist\, 210 Massachusetts Avenue
 \, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/tour-the-first-church-of-christ-scien
 tist-boston/78407/
END:VEVENT
