BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Boston 250 Pass
DTSTART:20260406T000000
DTEND:20261231T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:f5ec561aecebb0be6c4df415dd634d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:As the United States marks 250 years since the Declaration of 
 Independence in 1776\, five Boston landmarks have joined to create the BOS
 TON 250 PASS\, providing access to five iconic museums and historic church
 es on a single ticket! This special offer grants discounted adult admissio
 n (ages 18+) to five must-see historic sites in Downtown Boston: Paul Reve
 re House (1680)\, oldest surviving structure in Downtown Boston and home o
 f the renowned silversmith and political activist\; Old State House (1713)
 \, Boston's oldest public building\, witness to Boston Massacre in 1770 an
 d first reading of the Declaration of Independence in Boston\; Old North C
 hurch (1723)\, Boston's oldest surviving church building\, which famously 
 held aloft signal lanterns of the Midnight Ride in 1775\; Old South Meetin
 g House (1729)\, largest indoor meeting space in Colonial Boston and origi
 n site of the milestone Boston Tea Party in 1773\; King's Chapel (1754)\, 
 home of the first Anglican congregation in Boston and oldest pulpit in con
 tinuous use in the United States of America. PLEASE NOTE: 0.8 miles walkin
 g distance between five locations Accessible: King's Chapel\, Old South\, 
 Revere House Not accessible: Old State House\, Old North Church Public tra
 nsit: Gov't Center\, State\, and Haymarket Confirm visitor hours(hours var
 y) Valid for one week (7 days total) Do not purchase if listed below: Chil
 dren (ages 0-17) U.S. Military (active or retired) Groups of 10+ (reservat
 ion req'd) MA Teachers (MTA and BTU) MBTA Employees (plus guest) WGBH\, NE
 MA\, AAM\, ICOM Member WIC and EBT Cardholders (Discounts may already be a
 vailable\; please inquire at each location) Click here to purchase your Bo
 ston 250 Pass\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.
 com/event/boston-250-pass/89995/
LOCATION:Hub Town Tours\, Citywide\, Boston\, MA\, 02108
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/boston-250-pass/89995/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
