 r City’s leading cultural institutions to help Boston school-aged childr
 en feel at home in places that can expand their learning and show them the
  world. Through Boston Family Days\, all students who live in Boston (grad
 es K-12 and Boston Pre-K) and two guests can explore many of the City's cu
 ltural institutions for free on the first and second Sunday of each month 
 until December 2026. In addition\, Boston students and their families also
  have free access to live performances at Boston’s premier venues. Stude
 nts who are registered for Boston Family Days will receive ticket reservat
 ion links and instructions from the City before the performances. Particip
 ating institutions include: Boston Children's Museum Franklin Park Zoo Ins
 titute of Contemporary Art Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum John F. Kennedy
  Memorial Library and Museum MassArt Art Museum Museum of African American
