BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Your Spirit Guide
DTSTART:20260809T000000
DTEND:20261101T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:300b57f3f8caff46728c59d1b20287@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:What if you could create a guide to help you navigate life's c
 hallenges\, celebrate your strengths\, and honor your imagination? Join ar
 tist and educator Michelle de Celia (aka Koza) for a creative journey that
  combines visual art\, poetry\, performance\, and community connection. Th
 rough a series of hands-on workshops\, participants will explore cultural 
 traditions\, personal symbolism\, and storytelling to create a unique "spi
 rit guide" that reflects their inner wisdom\, creativity\, and aspirations
 . Using watercolor\, collage\, paper arts\, jewelry-making\, creative writ
 ing\, and performance exercises\, participants will develop an original ar
 twork and poem inspired by their spirit guide. Along the way\, Worcester-a
 rea guest artists will share their expertise and creative practices. Digi 
 Chivetta will lead visual arts explorations grounded in symbolism and inte
 rdisciplinary artmaking\; Teree Thomas-Perez\, founder of The Jewelry Co-o
 p\, will introduce jewelry-making and craft-based approaches to personal e
 xpression\; Laura DiCaronimo will guide participants through poetry and cr
 eative writing\; and Karina Beleño will lead performance activities that 
 help participants bring their spirit guides to life through movement\, voi
 ce\, and presence. The project culminates in a public exhibition and showc
 ase where participants can share their artwork\, poetry\, and creative dis
 coveries with family\, friends\, and the wider community. No previous art
 \, writing\, or performance experience is required. All materials will be 
 provided. Participants of all ages are welcome\, making this a family-frie
 ndly opportunity to create\, reflect\, and connect through art. Children u
 nder 14 should be accompanied by an adult. The class does not meet on 9/13
 . Come discover the guide waiting within you. This program is supported in
  part by a grant from the Worcester Arts Council\, a local agency\, which 
 is supported by the Mass Cultural Council\, a state agency.\n\nSources: Di
 scover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www.discovercentralma.or
 g/event/finding-your-spirit-guide/30235/
LOCATION:The Village Worcester\, 4 King St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01610
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/finding-your-spirit-guide/3023
 5/
END:VEVENT
