UID:038838c63e2bb8f8d9367c389ee683@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Boston's oldest neighborhood finally has a museum of its own! 
 Explore\, learn\, and uncover the rich history that makes the North End un
 ique. Step inside the North End Historical Museum at 3 Prince Street and w
 alk through four centuries of the people\, streets\, and stories that shap
 ed the North End. From colonial wharves to revolutionary meeting houses\, 
 from immigrant tenements to today's Little Italy\, the North End has been 
 continuously lived in longer than almost anywhere in America. The museum b
 rings that whole arc under one roof. We are a short walk from Old North Ch
 urch and Paul Revere's House\, right on the Freedom Trail. Stop in on your
  way through the neighborhood\, then stay for a cannoli! HOURS: 10:30 AM -
  5:00 PM (Tuesday - Sunday) EXTENDED NORTH END FEAST HOURS: Open until 8:3
 0 pm (Friday and Saturdays) LEARN MORE / VISIT TODAY\n\nSources: Meet Bost
 on\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/now-open%3a-north-end-his
 torical-museum/92430/
LOCATION:North End Historical Museum\, 3 Prince Street\, Boston\, MA\, 021
 13
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/now-open%3a-north-end-historical-muse
 um/92430/
