BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Plimoth Patuxet Museums
DTSTART:20260822T000000
DTEND:20260822T020000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:42cb9e0b1a34524f0c0765e3d54ced@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Plimoth Patuxet Museums explores the complex and interwoven st
 ories of English and Indigenous cultures in the 17th century through immer
 sive and experiential outdoor and indoor learning environments. The museum
  includes a reconstructed 1627 Pilgrim Village\, where costumed role-playe
 rs portray the Plymouth colonists (the “Pilgrims”) in their daily live
 s\; the Historic Patuxet Homesite where guests learn about the Wampanoag h
 eritage of the Northeast from contemporary interpreters who discuss the 17
 th-century life-ways of a culture that continues to thrive today. One Muse
 um. Four immersive exhibits. Endless possibilities to discover. Plan your 
 visit to Plimoth Patuxet Museums today. Open now through the Sunday follow
 ing Thanksgiving day. Hours Plimoth Patuxet 7 days a week | 9:00 a.m. - 5:
 00 p.m. Admission tickets sold daily until 4:15 p.m. Mayflower II 7 days a
  week | 9:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Admission tickets sold daily until 4:30 p.m.
  Plimoth Grist Mill 7 days a week | 9:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. Admission ticket
 s sold daily until 4:30 p.m.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://
 www.meetboston.com/event/plimoth-patuxet-museums/83010/
LOCATION:Plimoth Patuxet Museums\, 137 Warren Avenue\, Plymouth\, MA\, 023
 60
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/plimoth-patuxet-museums/83010/
END:VEVENT
