BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Harper Lee's To Kill a Mockingbird
DTSTART:20261008T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:1a23bfd6d4470eafa6add68d9daa9d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Harper Lee’s enduring classic To Kill a Mockingbird is adapt
 ed anew as Aaron Sorkin\, the brilliant and beautifully idealistic creator
  of The West Wing and A Few Good Men\, returns to writing for the stage. W
 hen upstanding lawyer Atticus Finch seeks justice for a wrongfully accused
  man\, he is tested by the limits of his virtue and the uneasy work of for
 giveness in a world ruptured in two. Harper Lee’s Pulitzer Prize–winni
 ng novel has resonated powerfully for over six decades. What does it mean 
 to revisit this beloved classic today with fresh eyes — to consider how 
 far we’ve come\, and how far we still need to go? Artistic Director Lore
 tta Greco creates the first regional production of Sorkin’s soaring adap
 tation\, especially for Boston.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https
 ://www.meetboston.com/event/harper-lees-to-kill-a-mockingbird/90291/
LOCATION:Huntington Theatre\, 264 Huntington Ave\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/harper-lees-to-kill-a-mockingbird/902
 91/
END:VEVENT
