BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ghosts and Gravestones Tour
DTSTART:20261026T000000
DTEND:20261026T020000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:710a5724b4a130cb77a094170e5cf3@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Recurring daily. What do you get when you combine a cursed pri
 vateer\, a pyromaniac circus ringleader\, a demon spat out of the pits of 
 Hades\, a homicidal opera diva\, and a deranged nanny? An experience unlik
 e anything else in Boston! Those are just a few of our guides who will dra
 g you kicking and screaming through Boston's sordid past. Never was there 
 a more treacherous lot of characters – each one dying to tell you tales 
 of Boston's dead in their own unusual way. There are so many of us that ea
 ch time you take our ghost tour\, you'll have a startling new experience. 
 So join us again and again! You will never know with whom you will be trap
 ped. Explore some of Boston's most haunted sites Walk amongst the dead in 
 burying grounds nearly 400 years old Exclusive night-time access into two 
 of Boston's oldest burying grounds See Boston's most haunted hotel: The Om
 ni Parker House Trolly and Walking Tours The Ghosts & Gravestones tour is 
 a hybrid experience that features both a themed trolley ride and guided wa
 lking segments. You will travel through the city’s most sordid streets a
 board the Trolley of the Doomed before stepping off for two 20-minute walk
 ing tours. We recommend wearing comfortable shoes so you don’t become 
 “dead on your feet.” Where to Find Us: Ghosts & Gravestones Frightseei
 ng Tour boards beside the Marriott Long Wharf Hotel on 200 Atlantic Avenue
 \, corner of State Street.\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://ww
 w.meetboston.com/event/ghosts-and-gravestones-tour/93962/
LOCATION:Ghosts and Gravestones of Boston\, Marriott Long Wharf Hotel\, co
 rner of State Street 200 Atlantic Avenue\, Boston\, MA
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/ghosts-and-gravestones-tour/93962/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Watercolor & Pen : Recipe Illustration
DTSTART:20261026T000000
DTEND:20271206T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:dd348aacd14e50f8dae4ac9bbf8214@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:This six-week\, project-based class is designed for students w
 ho have had an introduction to the basics of watercolor and are looking to
  continue their practice. All projects will be centered around illustratin
 g food and drink recipes in a variety layouts. The class covers how to pai
 nt various ingredients and how to arrange them into strong compositions. E
 ach project will include guidance for color matching\, a step by step walk
 through for the portrait and highlight specific painting and linework tech
 niques for this subject. All projects are designed to be traced in Micron 
 Pen before painting to add contrast and technical detail to the portrait. 
 No drawing experience required. Prerequisite: Introduction to Watercolor D
 ates: Weekly from October 26 - December 7 Meets: Mondays from 6:00 PM to 9
 :00 PM\n\nSources: Discover Central Massachusetts\nEvent page: https://www
 .discovercentralma.org/event/watercolor-%26-pen-%3a-recipe-illustration/30
 564/
LOCATION:Worcester Center for Crafts\, 25 Sagamore Rd.\, Worcester\, MA\, 
 01605
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/watercolor-%26-pen-%3a-recipe-
 illustration/30564/
END:VEVENT
