DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:7483d42f5982f8de5970df9b09f57d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us in October & November for weekly homeschool programs e
 xploring the stories of The Crane Estate & Appleton Farms. Participants wi
 ll learn the stories of the many people & animals who have lived here over
  the years from Indigenous farmers & fishers\, to European colonists\, to 
 local & invasive plant & animal species. Through inquiry and hands-on inve
 stigation we will learn what makes the Crane Estate & Appleton Farms speci
 al to their many residents & visitors\, including you! This is a drop-off 
 program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group work specia
 lized activities based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age
  groups. The class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent out
 doors as possible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and brin
 g a lunch and water bottle. Homeschool Scholars: Stories of the Farm & Coa
 st- This 4-class series program takes place on Thursday mornings from 9am-
 12pm on October 29\, November 5\, 12\, & 19. Crane Estate: October 29 & No
 vember 12 Appleton Farms: November 5 & 19\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEve
 nt page: https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-scholars-stories-of-th
 e-farm-coast/2026-10-29/
