BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Lighting the Landscape
DTSTART:20261031T000000
DTEND:20261128T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:f81a9c9980975428248f16341a107c@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A New Englander in home\, heritage\, and spirit\, Harley Bartl
 ett has dedicated himself to Northeastern landscapes for over 30 years. Th
 e marshy coast of the Narragansett Bay and the deep forests and grand tree
 s of the Great North Woods of the Adirondack Mountains are replete with me
 mories going back to a childhood influenced by both art and the outdoors. 
 Though whether he captures the landscape or the landscape captures him is 
 a valid question. "I respond to the visual world much in the same manner t
 hat music can have to our emotional soul. I find that something will trigg
 er a visual response and I work to capture that in my pictures\," says the
  artist. Most of his paintings begin with a swiftly executed plein-air ske
 tch\, but the real work takes place in the studio\, where the artist is in
  complete control of design\, composition\, color\, and paint application.
  LEARN MORE\n\nSources: Meet Boston\nEvent page: https://www.meetboston.co
 m/event/lighting-the-landscape/93804/
LOCATION:The Guild of Boston Artists\, The Guild of Boston Artists 162 New
 bury Street\, Boston\, MA\, 02116
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/lighting-the-landscape/93804/
END:VEVENT
