 a de Muertos\, bringing together culture\, tradition\, music\, dance\, and
  community! ✨ FREE & OPEN TO ALL COMMUNITY MEMBERS Bring your family\, f
 riends\, and pets! Everyone is welcome — especially those who come dress
 ed as a Catrina or Catrín! 📅 Sunday\, November 1\, 2026 ⏰ 1:00 – 5
 :00 PM 📍 Chelsea Square Park 179 Winnisimmet St.\, Chelsea\, MA 🌼 WH
 AT TO EXPECT: Enjoy a vibrant celebration featuring a Catrinas & Catrines 
 Parade\, live music\, folkloric dances\, food vendors\, face painting\, an
 d plenty of opportunities to celebrate and honor Día de Muertos tradition
 s with our community. The Veronica Robles Cultural Center (VROCC) proudly 
 presents the 2026 Día de Muertos Official Celebration in collaboration wi
 th the City of Chelsea\, with the support of the Chelsea Cultural Council
 \, a local agency supported by the Massachusetts Cultural Council. 🌼
