BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Santiago Cañón-Valencia\, cello
DTSTART:20261101T150000
DTEND:20261101T170000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:2253e0c3eea081b608272282f2c66f@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Colombian cellist Santiago Cañón-Valencia is an internationa
 lly acclaimed soloist\, composer\, and recording artist recognized for his
  expressive depth and technical brilliance. Described by The Strad as “t
 echnically flawless… totally under the skin of the composers’ idioms\,
 ” he will perform works of Debussy\, Ginastera\, Shostakovich\, and more
 . Program DEBUSSY: Sonate in D minor\, L. 135 GINASTERA: Cello Sonata\, Op
 . 49 PÄRT: Fratres CAÑON-VALENCIA: Ad Noctem SHOSTAKOVICH: Cello Sonata 
 in D minor\, Op. 40 Born in Bogotá in 1995\, he made his orchestral debut
  at just six years old with the Orquesta Filarmónica de Bogotá and has s
 ince built a global career spanning major concert halls and orchestras. A 
 BBC New Generation Artist (2022)\, Cañón-Valencia has performed with lea
 ding ensembles including the BBC Symphony Orchestra\, Brussels Philharmoni
 c\, Vienna Radio Symphony Orchestra\, and Seoul Philharmonic\, as well as 
 orchestras throughout the Americas and Europe. His 2025–2026 season feat
 ures engagements with the San Francisco Symphony\, Kansas City Symphony\, 
 and Camerata Pacifica\, alongside international recitals and festival appe
 arances. A prizewinner at major competitions—including Silver Medalist a
 nd Audience Favorite at the 2019 International Tchaikovsky Competition—h
 e is also a passionate advocate for new music\, regularly premiering and c
 ommissioning works by contemporary composers. As a recording artist\, his 
 releases range from core repertoire to original compositions\, including h
 is debut on Deutsche Grammophon and his album Ascenso\, highlighting Latin
  American voices. Equally dedicated to artistic exploration\, Cañón-Vale
 ncia’s work reflects a broad creative vision that extends beyond perform
 ance into composition and the visual arts.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEv
 ent page: https://northofboston.org/event/santiago-canon-valencia-cello/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/santiago-canon-valencia-cello/
END:VEVENT
