SUMMARY:Gifts for Good 2026: Alternative Gift Market
DTSTART:20261107T000000
DTEND:20261107T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:6ad5fcb9928ba02aab3c616c7fb9ac@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:OUR MISSION SOCIALLY RESPONSIBLE GIFT GIVING Alternative Gift 
 Market Cape Cod's (AGM) mission is to raise funds for worthy local\, natio
 nal and international organizations that are dedicated to improving the li
 ves of people and the health of our planet. These organizations work tirel
 essly to combat the effects of persistent poverty\, injustice and climate 
 change. Each year AGM's Steering Committee\, comprised of representatives 
 of the sponsoring religious organizations\, chooses the charities to parti
 cipate in the market. This year’s market includes nine local nonprofits
 \, working on Cape Cod or elsewhere in Massachusetts. In addition\, there 
 are four national nonprofits that work throughout the United States and si
 x global nonprofits that address problems in other parts of the world. One
  of the nonprofits addresses a problem that is challenging the entire worl
 d. Saturday Nov. 7 from 10am to 3pm Sunday Nov. 8 from 11am to 3pm Monday 
 Nov. 9 to 16 Online Learn More HERE. "There are two ways spreading light. 
 To be the candle or the mirror that reflects it."Edith Wharton AGM aims to
  be the mirror for worthy organizations\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEven
 t page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/gifts-for-good-2026%3a-altern
 ative-gift-market/52651/
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/gifts-for-good-2026%3a-alternativ
 e-gift-market/52651/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Giocosa Chamber Music: Practice makes Perfect
DTSTART:20261107T000000
DTEND:20261107T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:34e1ae3a1a962f7348e6b26c5a9e3e@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Practice is something that most of us do - whether it's gratit
 ude\, pickleball or piano - and sometimes practice can affect our lives in
  unexpected ways. In November\, we'll take a look at the art of practice -
  how it shaped the careers of Johannes Brahms and Clara Schumann\, how a s
 imple scale can be crafted into compelling music\, and whether Yoda’s 
 “Do or do not\, there is no try” actually applies. All through the len
 s of the music\, of course\, which includes works by Brahms\, Duparc\, Moz
 etich and Schumann.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/giocosa-chamber-music%3a-practice-makes-perfect/5
 2582/
LOCATION:Giocosa Chamber Music\, 3 River Rd\, Orleans\, MA\, 02653
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/giocosa-chamber-music%3a-practice
 -makes-perfect/52582/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:HOMECOMING Drag Show starring Laila McQueen
DTSTART:20261107T203000
DTEND:20261107T230000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:5688ea5622aec1d2f7fbbd55326377@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Who says you can’t go home again? Queendom Talent and The Cu
 t are excited to announce: HOMECOMING starring Laila McQueen\, Saturday\, 
 November 7th. For the first time since Summer 2024\, Laila returns to the 
 city that raised her for a night of high octane drag performances! With a 
 cast of New England’s best\, and an additional headliner to be announced
  later! Your hometown diva\, EMMY winner and star of RuPaul’s Drag Race 
 season 8: LAILA MCQUEEN! Laila McQueen is the stage name of Gloucester-bor
 n &r raised Tyler Devlin. Tyler competed as Laila on the MTV reality compe
 tition show RuPaul‘s Drag Race in 2016. He went on to perform the world 
 over in countries including Canada\, the UK\, Ireland\, France\, Italy\, t
 he Netherlands\, Australia and New Zealand. In 2020 he became a make-up ar
 tist on HBO’s uplifting drag makeover docuseries We’re Here for which 
 he won the EMMY award for “Outstanding Makeup for a Variety\, Nonfiction
  or Reality Program” in 2022 and for which he was again nominated in 202
 4. Meet your host: Kris Knievil\, a beloved fixture of Boston’s drag sce
 ne since the late ’90s\, Kris Knievil is known for her buxom blonde allu
 re and commanding stage presence. As former program director at Boston’s
  storied drag bar\, Jacques Cabaret\, Kris brings years of experience\, we
 ll timed and hilarious stories and boundless charisma to the stage\, ensur
 ing an evening of laughter and fun! And welcome to the stage Doriann Blonc
 h\, a Puerto Rican-born drag diva based in Boston\, known as The Beauty En
 chantment\, Doriann returns to Gloucester! She is a prominent figure in th
 e Boston scene at iconic parties like “Drag Me to Brunch” at Carrie Na
 tion\,” “LatinX Wednesdays” at Legacy\, and RuPaul’s Drag Race vie
 wing parties at Dani’s Queer Bar. And your crowned Miss All American God
 dess Ivy League. Ivy\, a native New Englander\, has performed all over the
  country in the Continental and All American Goddess pageantry systems. A 
 breathtaking live-singer a d broadway loving baby\, always turns the audie
 nce out with her emotional and energetic performances which hold audiences
  captivated!\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofbosto
 n.org/event/homecoming-drag-show-starring-laila-mcqueen/
LOCATION:The Cut\, 177 Main Street\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homecoming-drag-show-starring-laila-mc
 queen/
END:VEVENT
