BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261107T110000
DTEND:20261107T170000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:04e5633cb2ae93856105af74ca0b0a@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-11-07/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-11-07/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renaissance Faire at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261107T090000
DTEND:20261107T170000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:6cc32ea1c135a95cd3ddb5c5056b61@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of knights\, artisans\, performers\, and mer
 riment as Hammond Castle Museum transforms into one of New England’s mos
 t unique and immersive Renaissance celebrations. Experience the North Shor
 e’s own Renaissance Faire at Hammond Castle Museum\, where the Museum’
 s Medieval architecture and dramatic setting create an unforgettable backd
 rop for a day immersed in Renaissance culture\, history\, fantasy\, music
 \, and adventure. Enjoy the excitement of The Brotherhood of the Arrow and
  Sword‘s high-energy armored combat demonstrations\, bringing the mediev
 al battlefield to life. Listen in as our Curatorial Director\, John Leysat
 h\, presents on the History of Medieval Arms & Armor. Enjoy captivating pe
 rformances for wandering artists\, including a storyteller\, a harpist\, a
  bubble faery\, and other enchanting entertainers. Plus\, little ones will
  enjoy our kids’ tent offering little princes and princesses crafts for 
 hands-on fun. We’re thrilled to announce that James B. Jones and Shelley
  Wolfe from the Emmy Award-winning Netflix series Love on the Spectrum hav
 e agreed to return as the King and Queen of our 2026 Renaissance Faire! Th
 e couple will be on-site on Saturday\, November 7th\, and will be availabl
 e for photos! Cosplay dress-up is encouraged for all ages\, but weapons of
  any kind are prohibited and will not be permitted on campus. Your admissi
 on includes access to the interior of the Museum and free access to all sc
 heduled entertainment. (*Vendor services are not included. ) Little ones a
 ges 4 and under are free\, but require a reserved ticket\, and kids ages 5
  – 12 are just $10! Museum Members enjoy presale access to admission tic
 kets. Off-site parking is required\, and free shuttles will be running all
  day. Free parking will be available at Stage Fort Park (24 Hough Ave\, Gl
 oucester\, MA 01930)\, with complimentary shuttles running continuously be
 tween the park and the Museum from 8:45 AM to 5:00 PM. All ticket sales ar
 e final and non-transferable between the Faire dates. This is a major fund
 raiser for the nearly century-old Museum\, which is listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places. All proceeds from this event support the ong
 oing restoration and preservation of the Museum. The Museum is not handica
 pped accessible due to the many stairs on the Museum grounds and within th
 e Museum.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.o
 rg/event/renaissance-faire-at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-11-07/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/renaissance-faire-at-hammond-castle-mu
 seum/2026-11-07/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
