BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Giocosa Chamber Music: Practice makes Perfect
DTSTART:20261108T000000
DTEND:20261108T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:f11a40ef4d6cb7994b63559a6aed6d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Practice is something that most of us do - whether it's gratit
 ude\, pickleball or piano - and sometimes practice can affect our lives in
  unexpected ways. In November\, we'll take a look at the art of practice -
  how it shaped the careers of Johannes Brahms and Clara Schumann\, how a s
 imple scale can be crafted into compelling music\, and whether Yoda’s 
 “Do or do not\, there is no try” actually applies. All through the len
 s of the music\, of course\, which includes works by Brahms\, Duparc\, Moz
 etich and Schumann.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/giocosa-chamber-music%3a-practice-makes-perfect/5
 2581/
LOCATION:650 Main Street\, Chatham\, MA\, 02633
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/giocosa-chamber-music%3a-practice
 -makes-perfect/52581/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Jesse Cook
DTSTART:20261108T170000
DTEND:20261108T190000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:8606049a63d7b2cc4a62e2d1fcdbed@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:A global artist in every sense of the word\, Jesse Cook redefi
 nes music’s power to connect people across cultures and continents. Over
  the last three decades\, the Paris-born\, Toronto-raised master of the Sp
 anish guitar has built a devoted following for his spellbinding rumba flam
 enco\, routinely selling out performance halls from London to Los Angeles
 \, Milan to Montreal. On stage\, Cook radiates infectious energy\, collabo
 rating with his band and guest instrumentalists to craft immersive\, unfor
 gettable experiences. His concerts are celebrated for their warmth\, preci
 sion\, and emotional depth. Throughout his decades-long career\, Jesse Coo
 k has remained devoted to musical exploration. His boundary-defying artist
 ry has introduced flamenco and world music to wider audiences while mainta
 ining a signature style that is both technically masterful and soulfully e
 xpressive. That authenticity has clearly resonated—with over a billion s
 treams and views across platforms to date—proving his sound remains as r
 elevant as it is revered.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https:/
 /northofboston.org/event/jesse-cook-2/
LOCATION:Shalin Liu Performance Center\, 37 Main Street\, Rockport\, MA\, 
 01966
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/jesse-cook-2/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Newburyport Art presents May Exhibitions at 65 Water Street
DTSTART:20261108T110000
DTEND:20261108T170000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:655aac5e8fc10e825ffafef6a3dbad@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Newburyport Art (NAA) presents three new shows opening in the 
 month of May! Soft Structures is a group exhibition that explores fibers a
 nd fibrous material as process and metaphor. This exhibit features over 80
  artworks in a variety of media including drawing\, painting\, sculpture\,
  weaving\, embroidery\, quilting\, collage\, mixed media and more. This ex
 hibit is on view in the first-floor Sargent Gallery and second-floor Harts
 on Gallery. FOLIA is a collaborative exhibition featuring works by Amesbur
 y artists Amy Vander Els & Heather Karp. This exhibit explores the quiet b
 eauty and joyful rhythm of leaves and the symbolic meaning behind many tha
 t speaks of perseverance\, resilience and hope. Thirty-six artworks are di
 splayed amongst spring greenery in the first-floor Hills Gallery. Amy and 
 Heather will give a free artist talk on Thursday\, May 21st from 6:00-7:00
 pm\, concluding with Q&A. The 11th Annual Outdoor Sculpture Garden Exhibit
 ion debuted on May 1st\, and will remain on view year-round until April 20
 27. At nearly 3\,000 square feet\, the Range Lights Sculpture Garden resid
 es behind the historic NAA and is seen and visited by hundreds of people e
 very week. This year’s exhibition features 16 pieces by 10 local and reg
 ional artists. The participating artists include\; Jeffrey Briggs\, Lindle
 y Briggs\, Sarah Burns and Mike Platt\, Alexis Guieb-Alimbuyuguen\, Andrew
  Henschel\, Mae Kenny\, Evan Ralph\, Michael Updike and Raynor Warner. A r
 eception for FOLIA and Soft Structures will be held on Saturday\, May 2nd 
 from 4-6pm\, with the 11th Annual Sculpture Exhibit reception beginning at
  3:00pm\, including a Best in Show award at 3:30pm. The receptions are fre
 e and open to the public\, and visitors participating in the May 2nd Newbu
 ryport Artwalk are encouraged to stop by. New Hours: Wednesday through Sun
 day from 11:00am–5:00pm. The gallery is handicap accessible. More inform
 ation\, as well as an online gallery is available at newburyportart.org. F
 ounded in 1948\, Newburyport Art\, a 501(c)(3) non-profit\, is dedicated t
 o promoting and exhibiting members’ work and to providing art education 
 and access to the visual arts for the entire community. The gallery and ev
 ents are free and open to the public.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent p
 age: https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibiti
 ons-at-65-water-street/2026-11-08/
LOCATION:Newburyport Art Association\, 65 Water St\, Newburyport\, MA\, 01
 950
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/newburyport-art-presents-may-exhibitio
 ns-at-65-water-street/2026-11-08/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Renaissance Faire at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261108T090000
DTEND:20261108T170000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:db0505177d40aa75d528d7fc3ac722@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step into a world of knights\, artisans\, performers\, and mer
 riment as Hammond Castle Museum transforms into one of New England’s mos
 t unique and immersive Renaissance celebrations. Experience the North Shor
 e’s own Renaissance Faire at Hammond Castle Museum\, where the Museum’
 s Medieval architecture and dramatic setting create an unforgettable backd
 rop for a day immersed in Renaissance culture\, history\, fantasy\, music
 \, and adventure. Enjoy the excitement of The Brotherhood of the Arrow and
  Sword‘s high-energy armored combat demonstrations\, bringing the mediev
 al battlefield to life. Listen in as our Curatorial Director\, John Leysat
 h\, presents on the History of Medieval Arms & Armor. Enjoy captivating pe
 rformances for wandering artists\, including a storyteller\, a harpist\, a
  bubble faery\, and other enchanting entertainers. Plus\, little ones will
  enjoy our kids’ tent offering little princes and princesses crafts for 
 hands-on fun. We’re thrilled to announce that James B. Jones and Shelley
  Wolfe from the Emmy Award-winning Netflix series Love on the Spectrum hav
 e agreed to return as the King and Queen of our 2026 Renaissance Faire! Th
 e couple will be on-site on Saturday\, November 7th\, and will be availabl
 e for photos! Cosplay dress-up is encouraged for all ages\, but weapons of
  any kind are prohibited and will not be permitted on campus. Your admissi
 on includes access to the interior of the Museum and free access to all sc
 heduled entertainment. (*Vendor services are not included. ) Little ones a
 ges 4 and under are free\, but require a reserved ticket\, and kids ages 5
  – 12 are just $10! Museum Members enjoy presale access to admission tic
 kets. Off-site parking is required\, and free shuttles will be running all
  day. Free parking will be available at Stage Fort Park (24 Hough Ave\, Gl
 oucester\, MA 01930)\, with complimentary shuttles running continuously be
 tween the park and the Museum from 8:45 AM to 5:00 PM. All ticket sales ar
 e final and non-transferable between the Faire dates. This is a major fund
 raiser for the nearly century-old Museum\, which is listed on the National
  Register of Historic Places. All proceeds from this event support the ong
 oing restoration and preservation of the Museum. The Museum is not handica
 pped accessible due to the many stairs on the Museum grounds and within th
 e Museum.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.o
 rg/event/renaissance-faire-at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-11-08/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/renaissance-faire-at-hammond-castle-mu
 seum/2026-11-08/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tales & Ales (and Pies & Pints) at the Pearson Tavern
DTSTART:20261108T170000
DTEND:20261108T193000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:3e3ccfbef5984e524d93733f89dcf5@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Museum of Old Newbury for an evening that makes 17th-
 century court records wicked fun. Forget what you have been taught about t
 he 17th century. Court records reveal a world of complex\, modern\, and su
 rprising people. Their testimony reveals feuding neighbors\, scandalous ro
 mances\, tavern disturbances\, sharp tongues\, and spectacular lapses in j
 udgment (is that a chicken in your trousers?). Preserved in these records 
 are the words of ordinary people\, including women\, children\, servants\,
  and the enslaved\, whose voices are so often missing elsewhere\, demandin
 g justice\, asking for protection\, defending their reputations\, and accu
 sing their neighbors.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nor
 thofboston.org/event/tales-ales-and-pies-pints-at-the-pearson-tavern/
LOCATION:Pearson Tavern\, Byfield\, MA
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/tales-ales-and-pies-pints-at-the-pears
 on-tavern/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261108T111500
DTEND:20261108T161500
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:8bd9d6b71e39c181ebc01b6e750c8d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
