BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Homeschool Adventures: Session 1
DTSTART:20261117T130000
DTEND:20261117T160000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:6c350c9b08c2e3a6d8941f22c14adf@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Young explorers are invited to join us in September & October 
 for a 4-part homeschool series that will get them active & moving with nat
 ure adventures\, exercise\, and outdoor skill building. While exploring Ap
 pleton Farms & the Crane Estate\, participants complete active adventures 
 & design challenges that will exercise both their body & mind. Some potent
 ial activities include kayaking\, tide pooling\, wetland exploration\, ori
 enteering\, gardening\, obstacle course design\, and more! This is a drop-
 off program that is open to ages 5-11 and will include small group activit
 ies based on age and peer mentoring opportunities between age groups. The 
 class takes place rain or shine\, with as much time spent outdoors as poss
 ible. Students should arrive dressed for the weather and bring a lunch and
  water bottle. Homeschool Adventures: Session 1- This 4-class series progr
 am takes place on Tuesday afternoons from 1-4pm on September 15\, 22\, 29 
 & October 6. September 15: Tidepool & Shoreline Exploration at the Crane E
 state September 22: Kayaking Adventure at the Crane Estate September 29: P
 onding & Invasive Species Management at Appleton Farms October 6: Obstacle
  Course Design Challenge at Appleton Farms Tuition for the 4 classes is $2
 75 for Trustees Members and $325 for nonmembers. Registration covers all l
 isted session dates.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://nort
 hofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-11-17/
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/homeschool-adventures-session-1/2026-1
 1-17/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Museum Lecture and Live Demonstration: Calligraphy\, Community\, a
 nd the Declarations of Falmouth
DTSTART:20261117T000000
DTEND:20261117T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:21fc6711f56184c5f692a02a50516d@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:In this colorful presentation\, former White House chief calli
 grapher\, Rick Paulus\, takes you on a unique journey into the worlds of i
 nternational diplomacy\, White House entertaining and adventure on the hig
 h seas. Using his calligraphy as the backdrop\, Rick shares personal vigne
 ttes from working at the highest levels of government as a calligrapher\, 
 calligraphy’s role in diplomacy\, and many insights into the operations 
 of the White House Social Office. He will be incorporating some of the His
 torical Society’s archive pieces to show how calligraphy was used in Fal
 mouth for proclamations and special civic events. In 2006\, Rick took a bo
 ld leap by leaving his coveted position in Washington to explore new adven
 tures and art. It is here that Rick confronts his most difficult and most 
 rewarding assignments\; finding a voice for his work\, merging life into a
 rt and art into life\, and continuing to strive to achieve the technical s
 kills required to speak fluently from the hand. Today\, Rick continues his
  quest for the perfectly formed letter on the shores of Cape Cod\, Massach
 usetts. Admission: $40 Non-Members / $30 Museums on the Green Members Regi
 ster Here\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodcha
 mber.org/event/museum-lecture-and-live-demonstration%3a-calligraphy-commun
 ity-and-the-declarations-of-falmouth/52492/
LOCATION:Falmouth Museums on the Green\, 55 & 65 Palmer Avenue\, Falmouth
 \, MA\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/museum-lecture-and-live-demonstra
 tion%3a-calligraphy-community-and-the-declarations-of-falmouth/52492/
END:VEVENT
