BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Witch Trials: Bury to Salem — Live from the Museums
DTSTART:20261118T140000
DTEND:20261118T150000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:568dc19eeb9b6196101a6874dbf117@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a unique online event bringing together two museum
 s on opposite sides of the Atlantic to explore witch trials and folklore. 
 For this special evening\, Dan Clarke\, Heritage Officer at Moyse’s Hall
  Museum in Bury St Edmunds\, England and Rachel Christ-Doane\, Director of
  Education at the Salem Witch Museum\, will each take us behind the scenes
  of exhibits at their respective museums — live from the museums themsel
 ves. Dan and Rachel will use these exhibits as starting points to explore 
 the history\, beliefs\, stories and folklore surrounding witch trials\, of
 fering two fascinating perspectives on how witchcraft has been understood
 \, remembered and presented to the public. There is a remarkable historica
 l connection between the two museums. In 1662\, Amy Denny and Rose Cullend
 er were tried and executed for witchcraft at Bury St Edmunds. An account o
 f their trial\, A Tryal of Witches\, was published in 1682 and was later c
 onsulted in Salem during the 1692 witch trials. Moyse’s Hall Museum hold
 s a rare copy of this important account\, while the Salem Witch Museum tel
 ls the story of the trials that took place in Massachusetts three decades 
 later. This shared history has brought the two museums together in a speci
 al transatlantic partnership. In this event\, however\, the focus will be 
 on the exhibits\, witch trials and folklore — with Dan and Rachel each g
 iving us a live look at an object or exhibition from their own museum. The
 re will also be time for a Q&A\, giving you the opportunity to put your qu
 estions to Dan and Rachel.\n\nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https:
 //northofboston.org/event/witch-trials-bury-to-salem-live-from-the-museums
 /
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/witch-trials-bury-to-salem-live-from-t
 he-museums/
END:VEVENT
