END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Yin Yu Tang: A Chinese Home Tour
DTSTART:20261121T111500
DTEND:20261121T161500
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:6ad3c64c65872ee18b879dd5d9e9ed@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Step inside a 200-year-old Chinese home in Salem to experience
  Chinese art\, architecture and culture. For 200 years\, Yin Yu Tang stood
  in the rural village of Huang Cun in a mountainous region of southeastern
  China. Home to eight generations of the Huang family\, this house was dis
 mantled\, transported and re-erected at the Peabody Essex Museum in 2003 t
 hrough a partnership between PEM and the governmental authorities of Huizh
 ou\, in Anhui Province. Yin Yu Tang’s journey constitutes a landmark col
 laboration between Chinese and American architects\, artisans\, conservato
 rs\, engineers and museum experts. The home is presented as it was when th
 e family last lived there in 1982. Plan Your Visit Exercise care Please he
 lp us preserve the house for future generations by refraining from touchin
 g objects and the structure itself. Non-flash photography and videography 
 is permitted for personal use only. Tripods and selfie sticks are not allo
 wed. Please walk with care and watch out for uneven stonework and raised t
 hresholds. Store your belongings\, but keep your coat Yin Yu Tang is parti
 ally outdoors and may be cool in fall and winter. Strollers\, bags\, backp
 acks and umbrellas are not permitted in the house. Please leave them at th
 e coatroom or the cubbies by the Information desk. Our staff at the entran
 ce of the house can look after strollers. Pick up your audio guide in adva
 nce Please pick up your complimentary audio guide\, available in English a
 nd Mandarin\, at the Information desk 10 minutes before your visit. Please
  note: Plan to bring your own pair of headphones. Before your visit\, pres
 s #50 to listen to an introduction to the house. Once inside\, look for st
 one blocks with two-digit numbers. Press the number plus the play > button
  to hear the audio. Be prompt Please be at the doors to Yin Yu Tang five m
 inutes before your scheduled visit with your audio guide in hand. A staff 
 member will alert you shortly before the end of your time slot.\n\nSources
 : North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang
 -a-chinese-home-tour/2026-11-21/
LOCATION:Peabody Essex Museum\, East India Square\, 161 Essex Street\, Sal
 em\, MA\, 01970
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/yin-yu-tang-a-chinese-home-tour/2026-1
 1-21/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:You're a Good Man\, Charlie Brown
DTSTART:20261121T000000
DTEND:20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:efeeeed6bc9bbfe9c3dc7cead749b1@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:About You're a Good Man\, Charlie Brown Happiness is great mus
 ical theatre! With charm\, wit and heart\, You’re A Good Man\, Charlie B
 rown explores life through the eyes of Charlie Brown and his friends in th
 e Peanuts gang. This revue is a series of songs and vignettes\, based on t
 he beloved Charles Schulz comic strip. It is guaranteed to please audience
 s of all ages! YOU'RE A GOOD MAN\, CHARLIE BROWN is presented by arrangeme
 nt with Concord Theatricals on behalf of Tams-Witmark LLC. www.concordthea
 tricals.com Falmouth High School Theatre Company The goal of Falmouth High
  School Theatre Company is to inspire young actors and theatre technicians
  to express themselves through their shared passion for theatre arts. FHS 
 Theatre Company is a great place to meet new people and make lifelong memo
 ries and connections. A typical theatrical season includes fall and spring
  productions. All levels of talent and interest are welcome. You're a Good
  Man\, Charlie Brown Fri. Nov 20th 2026\, 7:00 pm Sat. Nov 21st 2026\, 2:0
 0 pm Sat. Nov 21st 2026\, 7:00 pm Sun. Nov 22nd 2026\, 2:00 pm Buy tickets
  HERE.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchambe
 r.org/event/youre-a-good-man-charlie-brown/52655/
LOCATION:Falmouth High School Auditorium 874 Gifford Street\, Falmouth\, M
 A\, 02540
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/youre-a-good-man-charlie-brown/52
 655/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:BLUES AFTERNOON: Jerry Portnoy talks life & music with Gregory Wil
 liams
DTSTART:20261122T000000
DTEND:20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:1ca39ebdf2f750cc73f9a93c23ad51@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Thacher Hall for A Blues Afternoon\, where Judge Gr
 egory Williams will interview legendary harmonica player\, Jerry Portnoy\,
  and explore the history of blues along the way. This multi-media program 
 will feature photos\, videos\, and music and conclude with a book sale and
  signing. Jerry Portnoy is a Grammy nominee and the ONLY musician to have 
 played in the fabled bands of both Muddy Waters and Eric Clapton. He grew 
 up in the crucible of electric blues: Chicago’s famed Maxwell Street Mar
 ket in the late 1940s and early ‘50s. He has performed at the White Hous
 e\, Carnegie Hall\, the Royal Albert Hall\, Radio City Music Hall\, the Sm
 ithsonian\, and at jazz festivals around the world in a career that has ta
 ken him to all fifty states and dozens of countries on six continents. In 
 a remarkable life\, he also ran the largest pool hall in Chicago\, did a s
 tint as a paratrooper\, lived in San Francisco during 1967’s famed “Su
 mmer of Love\,” assisted in surgery\, worked at Cook County Jail\, and d
 ined at Giorgio Armani’s home. He is pictured on the packaging for the M
 arine Band harmonica: the world’s most popular musical instrument. His r
 iveting autobiography/memoir Dancing with Muddy: Muddy Waters\, Eric Clapt
 on\, and My Lucky Life In and Out of the Blues was published in 2025 by Ch
 icago Review Press.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Chamber\nEvent page: https://www.
 capecodchamber.org/event/blues-afternoon%3a-jerry-portnoy-talks-life-%26-m
 usic-with-gregory-williams/52668/
LOCATION:Thacher Hall\, 266 Route 6A P.O. Box 237\, Yarmouth Port\, MA\, 0
 2675
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/blues-afternoon%3a-jerry-portnoy-
 talks-life-%26-music-with-gregory-williams/52668/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Deck the Halls at Hammond Castle Museum
DTSTART:20261122T090000
DTEND:20261122T153000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:409a9c5e8df2a4a84633aea8dd4e1b@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for the 2026 Holiday Season as we proudly present our 
 8th annual holiday celebration\, Deck the Halls\, a Museum-wide holiday in
 stallation! Travel back in time to a castle filled with candlelight and lu
 sh\, opulent textures inspired by the great medieval and Renaissance castl
 es of Europe. We are delighted to partner again with Elaine Quinn Interior
 s\, a boutique residential interior design firm based in Manchester-by-the
 -Sea\, to bring heightened inspiration and artistry to this year’s museu
 m-wide holiday installation. Abundant greenery and sumptuous layers of dé
 cor create a richly immersive seasonal experience throughout the Museum. W
 ander through rooms adorned with white birch and Christmas trees\, sparkli
 ng fairy lights\, hydrangea-lace garlands\, and elegant bows\, with each s
 pace transformed by its own unique holiday theme. This celebration also em
 braces the traditions of Hanukkah\, with two beautifully displayed menorah
 s adding their own warm glow to the Museum’s festive splendor. From natu
 re’s bounty of fruits and greenery to the warm glow of candlelight\, eve
 ry detail creates a feast for the senses. Along the way\, encounter a roya
 l guard of nutcrackers\, a gingerbread house replica of the Museum\, and p
 layful elves and gnomes up to mischief\, adding a touch of whimsy for litt
 le ones. In addition to the holiday installation\, guests can enjoy the te
 mporary exhibition\, “Brave-Too-Much”: The Legend of John Coffee Hays.
  Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to fully experience the h
 oliday installation and exhibition Extended Tuesday and Thursday Tour Hour
 s: New this year\, visitors can enjoy extended hours on Tuesdays and Thurs
 days\, with last entry at 7:15 p.m. These extended guided and self-guided 
 tour hours offer greater opportunities to experience the Museum after dark
 \, when holiday décor glows with flickering candlelight and twinkling lig
 hts. Upon arrival\, visitors will discover the path and outdoor Courtyard
 \, arches and towers aglow with festive holiday lighting\, creating a trul
 y magical seasonal atmosphere. Visitors will have more time to explore the
  Museum’s holiday decorations and experience the beauty of this historic
  site after dark. Admission pricing varies\, please visit our website for 
 accurate pricing. Guests should plan for approximately 60 minutes to take 
 in the full holiday grandeur. Museum member benefits apply.\n\nSources: No
 rth of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-
 at-hammond-castle-museum/2026-11-22/
LOCATION:Hammond Castle Museum\, 80 Hesperus Avenue\, Gloucester\, MA\, 01
 930
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/deck-the-halls-at-hammond-castle-museu
 m/2026-11-22/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ecumenical Thanksgiving Service in Historic Kelley Chapel
DTSTART:20261122T000000
DTEND:20261122T000000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:d6853d92237849ad0a24b9aa9fbaeb@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, November 22\, 3 PM – HSOY’s Ecumenical Thanksgivi
 ng Service in Historic Kelley Chapel . Enjoy the warmth of the potbellied 
 stove\, traditional hymns\, and a holiday message.\n\nSources: Cape Cod Ch
 amber\nEvent page: https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/ecumenical-thanksg
 iving-service-in-historic-kelley-chapel/52689/
LOCATION:Historical Society of Old Yarmouth\, 229 Route 6A 11 Strawberry L
 ane\, Yarmouth Port\, MA\, 02675
URL:https://www.capecodchamber.org/event/ecumenical-thanksgiving-service-i
 n-historic-kelley-chapel/52689/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Godspell
DTSTART:20261122T140000
DTEND:20261122T160000
DTSTAMP:20261029T174705Z
UID:6103eaf734dc15ff0620e968553459@massachusetts-events
DESCRIPTION:The North Shore Players\, a community theater in Danvers\, pre
 sents the musical “Godspell.” Based on the Gospel of St. Matthew\, mus
 ic includes “Day by Day” and “Prepare Ye the Way of the Lord.” Per
 formances are Nov. 20 and 21 at 7 p.m.\, and Nov. 22 at 2 p.m. Location is
  Hogan Regional Auditorium\, 450 Maple St.\, Danvers\, the old Danvers sta
 te hospital. Tickets $20-$25\, with group rates available. Tickets and dri
 ving directions are at www.northshoreplayersma.org. The North Shore Player
 s is a 501(c)3 non-profit\, and has been on the North Shore since 1957.\n
 \nSources: North of Boston\nEvent page: https://northofboston.org/event/go
 dspell/2026-11-22/
LOCATION:Hogan Regional Center Auditorium\, 450 Maple Street\, Danvers\, 0
 1923
URL:https://northofboston.org/event/godspell/2026-11-22/
END:VEVENT
